// RUN: not triton-metal-opt --convert-tritongpu-to-metal %s 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
//
// Phase B decoy: a CAUSAL-masked attention loop must not be claimed by
// tryFlashAttentionLoop. It is structurally identical to the multi-head kernel
// in flash_attention.mlir — 3 iter_args (rank-2 accumulator + running sum +
// running max), 2 tt.dot, 2 tt.reduce, one transposed dot operand, 1 tt.store,
// 1 arith.divsi (`d_head = d_model / h`) whose result feeds `pid1 * d_head` —
// so every gate that existed before Phase B passes. The only difference is one
// extra `arith.cmpi sle` term ANDed into the softmax mask:
//
//   logits_mask = (row < N) & (key < N) & (key <= row)
//
// `metal.flash_attention` has no causal mode, so claiming this loop emitted
// FULL attention with the causal term dropped. Measured against a per-head
// reference on MPS with the pre-Phase-B matcher: compiles clean, no
// diagnostic, maxerr 2.4. The Phase-B role walk rejects it at
// `maskIs(sel.getCondition(), {Row<N, Key<N})` — the extra term makes the
// collected mask a 3-element set. Run with TRITON_METAL_FA_DEBUG=1 to print
// "softmax mask is not exactly (row < N) & (key < N)".
//
// With FA declining, the loop falls through to the general path and hits the
// pre-existing L1d3 staged-transpose reject — a hard error, which is the
// correct outcome for a kernel this backend cannot express.
//
// The behavioural companion (reject OR numerically correct, for this variant
// plus an ALiBi bias and a sqrt-less scale) is
// test_flash_attention_rejects_near_miss_kernels in
// python/test/unit/test_metal_backend_flash_attention.py.
//
// CHECK-NOT: metal.flash_attention
// CHECK: error:
// CHECK-SAME: broader staged-transpose deferred to L1d3
// CHECK-NOT: metal.flash_attention
//
